{"id": "clm:969c372cf181de6dd2ef9046384dc477b0c9b30fe8bf8275231e32c705558561", "type": "statement", "text": "Inbound endpoint addresses support static or dynamic allocation. A dynamic address stays unchanged during normal operation but can change when the endpoint is reprovisioned, so forwarder configuration must account for that lifecycle. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spmonkey.com/azure-dns-private-resolver-hybrid-dns-runbook/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:baeeb654b917d99af1a701d46b5d2ab60ab28019ebcff9e17696773b235ba60f"]}
{"id": "clm:1f8040dcd77fc9a26952a5df1eb4f4e53a9db6e1f656f5627c0a0e16e01444f9", "type": "statement", "text": "Create only the endpoints required by query direction: inbound for external clients querying Azure-visible names; outbound plus forwarding rules for Azure queries sent to external DNS servers. Bidirectional deployments can need both. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-private-resolver-overview", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "how-to", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spmonkey.com/azure-dns-private-resolver-hybrid-dns-runbook/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8c493005ef32cbba0f6a03a8818c5c891379ef8f9995a11c4d91c65ef54ed325", "ev:de938336712d04061be53e1ccb652ca6c5d5f17eead680f186cccfdf2ab298a1"]}
{"id": "clm:a149af9902066b744176b89cac1dea62119cd0d52054ebcd16049356e7631e41", "type": "statement", "text": "Each resolver endpoint needs a separate, dedicated subnet delegated to Microsoft.Network/dnsResolvers. Microsoft documents supported endpoint subnet sizes from /28 through /24; the subnet cannot host another service. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-06-22)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-private-resolver-overview", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spmonkey.com/azure-dns-private-resolver-hybrid-dns-runbook/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:449f900f7419f42d2abd5289ff13072ee4c45dcf067e8d6afdd4351816717899", "ev:b0338a8f21141fff7b7da3685f04c35dac09d926e988cb001644f8639f0832e4"]}
{"id": "clm:c33a709e9f7fa7ff620c37eeec7015a626ee6af137a5a6105e56cf9fae7478c1", "type": "statement", "text": "An outbound endpoint uses a dedicated subnet but has no provisioned listener IP like an inbound endpoint; configure forwarding rulesets rather than pointing clients at an outbound endpoint IP. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bcc92d975cd3b2e33129f4abf18142d11dc6de6b821172b891ba7b59fac82a07"]}
{"id": "clm:aa124e429cddad0b76cfb512e2bfc901a3c13da7ea8372b585aad4caecc8a0a4", "type": "statement", "text": "Microsoft rejects 168.63.129.16 as a forwarding-rule destination with the error \"Exception while making add request for rule\". Use an appropriate reachable DNS server target rather than that Azure platform address. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spmonkey.com/azure-dns-private-resolver-hybrid-dns-runbook/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:72f3f694e88c709f0bd294c66b77ade5a6aadaea58ecd4ea6d723d115942dba7", "ev:c2d92d73fc27e3ff9bf55ab32f0e0d594b8332fe9f106c4944fbaf78ed7d6bf9"]}
{"id": "clm:ffa8c00e66d4753b3097afc8a4c6d76b0f527e05ae230ad66dc306e4468e5e13", "type": "statement", "text": "Chris Hailes provides an original Bicep deployment example containing resolver, inbound endpoint, outbound endpoint, forwarding ruleset, VNet link and forwarding-rule resources; the example illustrates the resource dependencies, rather than proving production readiness. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://blog.brewedinthecloud.com/p/azure-dns-privateresolver/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:939701f6d8574186394bbc62f670e40bc2fa4b90044d96de619e19cc59a50122", "ev:dff0998215ad75348a0e1c696ad853094885dadc0eb37e132dafd3b0b27c1b9d"]}
{"id": "clm:19f5f55b85cd12516513cbdb74524c6392b03e0989d29b20073963f190958b61", "type": "statement", "text": "Azure DNS Private Resolver provides managed recursive resolution and conditional forwarding between Azure and external networks; inbound endpoints receive queries, while outbound endpoints apply forwarding rulesets. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-private-resolver-overview", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2c5aae416714d8edaae771ab24139d4d1d0d6f3338c8f7d8ae97878892aaac6d", "ev:d7d738ee535549ad9d37d2e7fd7c79b1cf4803c53b6a419359cb7b0030789b43"]}
{"id": "clm:a9a3c16e151814ae48c07d72a9673922c22a9517d86faf177e135328c7103411", "type": "statement", "text": "An on-premises conditional forwarder targets the inbound endpoint's private IP over existing private connectivity. That endpoint resolves private zones linked to its own VNet. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-private-resolver-overview", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2c5aae416714d8edaae771ab24139d4d1d0d6f3338c8f7d8ae97878892aaac6d", "ev:98f6627444f61943a3015b9330280b4844620d994a8363043b796ade5a27c7ae"]}
{"id": "clm:ee3d40f609d9a47eeb11f41eebe434b0afbe635994fbff9b19a5b72529b76e71", "type": "statement", "text": "Azure clients using Azure-provided DNS consult linked private zones before forwarding rulesets. Matching forwarding rules use the most specific DNS suffix; unmatched queries proceed through Azure DNS. Custom VNet DNS settings send queries to the configured custom servers instead. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-private-resolver-overview", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spmonkey.com/azure-dns-private-resolver-hybrid-dns-runbook/", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:df00368d7e92a3f2869e64c3a4d6f0d77ee106f2e0916e74762dc6b0ba2f13b7"]}
{"id": "clm:a22c74bd9b701c5826743f646a74c6c79692c7c52cfdfed1f6170690bfa4496b", "type": "statement", "text": "A ruleset that forwards a namespace to an inbound endpoint must not be linked to that endpoint's own VNet: the configuration can create a DNS forwarding loop. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://naxaya.com/articles/azure-dns-private-resolver-diagnose-forwarding-loop-before-changing-zones/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:d72568b19b3fc066b14700a7d11974ae94ad5011ddca2b8e85c81c18ee4fb0ce"]}
{"id": "clm:e1d7b8ec23b06d50155a74956b39d6eeb8b212fb4b7077fb9ac14d71438cb758", "type": "statement", "text": "For Atlas, resolver deployment is conditional on DNS requirements, not an established universal prerequisite. This is a synthesis: Azure documents hybrid forwarding, while Atlas documents endpoint-specific connection strings resolving to private interface IPs. DNS success alone does not establish database connectivity. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-private-resolver-overview", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/faq/connection-changes.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1a539b47de879d3de311968d644b67c81aff4e0c4fafdd36c02518f4518b4082", "ev:34916ee1713a7c2e55f8cfb0c16777dbe06a1c96aa6d8b071018e07c94235e1c", "ev:4c0427fe5c420107d329cdaa37ab84cf562845af292be1ef10220b06d171b3f7"]}
{"id": "clm:913ba3d4c4035f2273b8bf36a8ced98a66d91521b6e4a2470b3467b06481e06b", "type": "statement", "text": "AzureRM provider 3.93.0 historically rejected private_ip_address for a Static inbound endpoint with \"Value for unconfigurable attribute\". Issue #25026 records the reproducer and closure through #25035 on March 4, 2024; this is historical provider behavior, not evidence of a current Azure service restriction. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-azurerm/issues/25026", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3ca3d4dc4b4707cc70ea2c065016c2b93c03317f999c4f18e13bc0386228b9da", "ev:654a113ec376e214a38a90a010c91e984669b65c87d168e1a1ada1e1424bd416"]}
{"id": "clm:773ebd8da4b129a5cf0b36232c8fd8e42a10beb2ffd41cf223a85c9c50f547b1", "type": "statement", "text": "Resolver endpoints require separate dedicated subnets delegated to Microsoft.Network/dnsResolvers; the parent resolver references one VNet, and each endpoint belongs within that resolver's network. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-private-resolver-overview", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:126490e504ceded00b9956959c06e6b36157eac832f7561324c67adde91f5462", "ev:bcc92d975cd3b2e33129f4abf18142d11dc6de6b821172b891ba7b59fac82a07", "ev:ec183103acf43903ef05610684e7b66130337e8dc35f53decb017dd64a1c2037"]}
{"id": "clm:fdf79638edee63c5ea8edf5359e17ae3af58184130b567864c1a0a3e7e61107c", "type": "statement", "text": "Azure DNS Private Resolver replaces self-managed DNS forwarding servers with managed inbound and outbound resolution between Azure and external private environments. Hybrid use still requires network connectivity, such as VPN or ExpressRoute. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/dns-private-resolver-overview", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://blog.brewedinthecloud.com/p/azure-dns-privateresolver/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:59dae4955b9f8b47070e5ea45e8d64fb7bc20e0942e02d02408336a9e4e00812"]}
{"id": "clm:a80c178454fe19a14005b8daf3bf3a5201b3b5f255b320a0e57d40cd274f6121", "type": "statement", "text": "An inbound endpoint exposes a private IP that external DNS servers can use as a conditional-forwarding target. It resolves private zones linked to the endpoint VNet. An outbound endpoint supplies forwarding egress and has no equivalent client-facing listener IP. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spmonkey.com/azure-dns-private-resolver-hybrid-dns-runbook/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2c5aae416714d8edaae771ab24139d4d1d0d6f3338c8f7d8ae97878892aaac6d", "ev:bcc92d975cd3b2e33129f4abf18142d11dc6de6b821172b891ba7b59fac82a07"]}
{"id": "clm:e1fef71d9bb3f1e83c8d6d19ce45f9828e7241eb686230c63a3c872ed526cdd5", "type": "statement", "text": "A forwarding rule targeting the resolver inbound endpoint must not be applied through a ruleset link to that inbound endpoint VNet: this can create a DNS forwarding loop. A wildcard rule also requires a target that can resolve public dependencies. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dns/private-resolver-endpoints-rulesets", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spmonkey.com/azure-dns-private-resolver-hybrid-dns-runbook/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:d72568b19b3fc066b14700a7d11974ae94ad5011ddca2b8e85c81c18ee4fb0ce"]}
{"id": "clm:34901724f9b48794e2e488bd7f9396aeaffb9ff39796670be3f829340ed98d04", "type": "statement", "text": "For DNS troubleshooting, repeat one FQDN and record type from affected and control networks. Record the actual resolver, response code, answer, TTL and timing; test UDP and TCP separately before attributing timeouts to a loop. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://naxaya.com/articles/azure-dns-private-resolver-diagnose-forwarding-loop-before-changing-zones/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Azure Private DNS Resolver"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://spmonkey.com/azure-dns-private-resolver-hybrid-dns-runbook/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:ec64b847415ce812eb90032b34f87772cdb87c780f195460d41d7ec5487463b6", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7dfdb51b02fbdc00148de3deaacaffba3695ce612bc4da50926da19221c7c235", "ev:9f3f7f87a4f4d3403833a0587f46e219dea29c70ab90e073d9339229cc15801e"]}
